ve Officer | Age 45 | Compensation: $603,798 (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $201K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $88K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["World Acceptance Corporation is a small-cap financial services business with a $581M market cap on $585M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $255M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 44 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 7.50\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 22.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 19% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (258.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.2pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 13% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $42.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 71% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Behavioral Patterns of WRLD and Institutional Flows","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/12/Behavioral_Patterns_of_WRLD_and_Institutional_Flows_112426075802_1795525082.html","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795525082.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.459,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Reviewing World Acceptance (NASDAQ:WRLD) & Upbound Group (NASDAQ:UPBD)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/16/reviewing-world-acceptance-nasdaqwrld-upbou